1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,650
quick-keys puts number-key shortcuts right above your Claude Code prompt.

2
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:09,850
Press one from an empty prompt, and slash code-review is typed in for you.

3
00:00:10,450 --> 00:00:15,150
Fill leaves the text for you to finish. Submit sends the turn on its own.

4
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:20,200
Install it with one command, pointing at the marketplace in this repo.

5
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:26,900
Run slash keys to edit them. One line binds a digit, a kind, a label, and the text.

6
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:31,950
MIT licensed. The four it ships with are meant to be replaced.
